{"name":"Horror Snob","hex":"#d34d4d","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"horror","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An intense distressing emotion of fear or repugnance.","Something horrible; that which excites horror."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/horror"},{"term":"snob","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who wishes to be seen as a member of the upper classes or of some other elite (such as the masters of a certain craft) and who looks down on those perceived to have inferior or unrefined tastes, skills, etc. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A cobbler or shoemaker."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/snob"}],"entries":[{"title":"Snob","blocks":[{"text":"Snob is a pejorative term for a person who feels superior due to their social class, education level, or social status in general; it is sometimes used especially when they pretend to belong to these classes. The word snobbery came into use for the first time in England during the 1820s."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Ward_McAllister_caricature_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Ward_McAllister_caricature_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Snob","wikidata":"Q728497"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/The_Snob_%281921%29_-_Ad_1.jpg/500px-The_Snob_%281921%29_-_Ad_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/The_Snob_%281921%29_-_Ad_1.jpg/500px-The_Snob_%281921%29_-_Ad_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ad for the American film The Snob, 1921 film with Wanda Hawley and Walter Hiers, on inside front cover of the January 30, 1921 Film Daily.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Snob_(1921)_-_Ad_1.jpg"}]